.TH PAM_HIRO 8 "August 2026" "HIRO" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
pam_hiro \- PAM module for HIRO face authentication
.SH SYNOPSIS
auth    sufficient    pam_hiro.so [socket=PATH] [timeout_ms=N] [debug]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBpam_hiro.so\fR asks the \fBhirod\fR(8) daemon for a face verdict for the
user being authenticated.
.PP
Verdict mapping:
.RS
.PD 0
.TP
face match
PAM_SUCCESS (with \fBsufficient\fR this skips the password)
.TP
no match
PAM_AUTH_ERR (password fallback proceeds)
.TP
daemon unreachable or camera unavailable
PAM_AUTHINFO_UNAVAIL (password fallback)
.TP
unexpected failure
PAM_SYSTEM_ERR
.RE
.PD
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B socket=PATH
Daemon socket (default \fI/run/hirod/hirod.sock\fR).
.TP
.B timeout_ms=N
Per-attempt cap in milliseconds (default 5000).
.TP
.B debug
Verbose logging via \fBpam_syslog\fR.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# Debian/Ubuntu: enable via pam-auth-update, or add to /etc/pam.d/sudo:
auth    sufficient    pam_hiro.so
.fi
.SH SECURITY
The module never holds the camera or templates, performs no recognition
itself, and never blocks login: on any failure the password path remains
available.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hiro (1),
.BR hirod (8),
.BR hiro.conf (5)
